  "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is a member of the set of integer numbers.\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $\u00acP(x)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The symbol \"$\u00ac$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is a member of the set of integer numbers.\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *not* a member of the set of integer numbers. Therefore, $\u00acP(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is **not** a member of the set of integer numbers.",
